# GPD Pocket 4 accelerometer orientation. Installed to
# /etc/udev/hwdb.d/61-sensor-local.hwdb.
#
# Corrects what iio-sensor-proxy reports so that EVERY desktop reads the true
# orientation. Without it the sensor lies about which way up the machine is, and
# each compositor needs its own daemon translating the lie - which is what
# home/dot_config/hypr/scripts/auto-rotate.sh was, and why rotation died the
# moment Hyprland was not running.
#
# Value taken from systemd issue 41036, where a maintainer worked it out with
# another Pocket 4 owner. That issue is closed. This machine is the same model:
#
#   /sys/class/dmi/id/sys_vendor   -> GPD
#   /sys/class/dmi/id/product_name -> G1628-04
#   accelerometer modalias         -> acpi:MXC6655:MXC6655:
#
# FORMATTING IS LOAD-BEARING. The match line starts at column 0 and the property
# line starts with EXACTLY ONE SPACE. hwdb silently ignores the entry otherwise,
# which presents as "the matrix did nothing" rather than as an error.
#
# Apply with:
#   systemd-hwdb update
#   udevadm trigger -p DEVNAME=/dev/iio:device0
#   systemctl restart iio-sensor-proxy
#
# Verify with `monitor-sensor --accel`, which must report:
#   laptop (keyboard toward you) -> right-up
#   rotated clockwise            -> normal
#   keyboard up                  -> left-up
#   keyboard right               -> bottom-up
#
# Those four are the CORRECTED readings for this hardware, per the same issue.
# They are also exactly what the old hand-calibrated auto-rotate.sh observed, so
# the note claiming this unit's sensor is uniquely mis-mounted looks wrong - the
# ArchWiki mapping is the outlier, not this machine. Confirm against hardware
# before trusting either statement.

sensor:modalias:acpi:MXC6655:*:dmi:*:svnGPD:pnG1628-04:*
 ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX=0, 1, 0; 1, 0, 0; 0, 0, -1
